{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated","id":989794,"title":"will rules on gargoyles get updated ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-19T02:39:20-07:00","id":989794,"title":"will rules on gargoyles get updated ?","content":"I wanted to know will rules on gargoyles and making them get updated ?<br /> <br /> If so will we be able to have rules for playing them. Me and a few others think it would be interesting to play a game of gargoyles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T04:24:21-07:00","id":989820,"title":"","content":"There are currently three books planned for Vampire. In SotC book, there's a Cruac ritual for creating a &quot;god.&quot; There's also a ghoul book and an elder book. I seriously doubt there would be anything approaching gargoyles in the elder book. There might be something in the ghoul book, but I haven't heard anything to that effect, so it could go either way. I do expect madragora and animal ghoul coverage there, so there is a bit of chance gargoyles might make an appearance as well. I wouldn't expect a lot of details, however.<br /> <br /> Now, while there were rules for <i>making</i> a gargoyle in 1e, there were never rules for <i>playing </i>one. I'm guessing that, since you're talking about playing gargoyles, you're actually refering to the pseudo-clan from Masquerade rather than the mostly mindless constructs? Requiem has never made any move towards that direction, and I have never heard of any suggestion to add them to Requiem's lore. The Cruac ritual in 1e as well as some rules in the hack-filled Dance Macabre book are the closest Requiem has ever had to gargoyles, and they haven't been exactly a big thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-19-2016, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:36:22-07:00","id":989865,"title":"","content":"Nope I was talking nothing about masquerade. I saw the rules for creating gargoyles and being I was not sure how well it would work in 2e I've been using the horror rules to make them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:37:35-07:00","id":989895,"title":"","content":"Then I dont' know if there's going to be rules you want. Because there's never been anything approaching playable gargoyles, not even with the Danse Macabre rules. It sounds like you're asking for an entirely different game, to be honest, given that gargoyles wouldn't have any Humanity to hold on to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:43:27-07:00","id":989896,"title":"","content":"Beast could be a better choose, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:15:53-07:00","id":989910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=989896#post989896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast could be a better choose, i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Promethean would come close, but gargoyles have always been a Requiem thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:05:21-07:00","id":989967,"title":"","content":"Well, given that wings and ability to turn to stone are Gargoyle's key features, the Requem 2E version of them appears to be Clan Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:07:04-07:00","id":990009,"title":"","content":"Gargoyles aren't usually fit to play, but I'm sure you could whip something up to make them playable. I once started writing up a Coil that's fifth level could create Gargoyles that would be playable if you gave them a Humanity track, but I never got beyond the outline phase. Someday hopefully I'll finish you Coil of Genesis!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:15:11-07:00","id":990015,"title":"","content":"They could also be a bloodline (possibly nosferatu) whose gifts are wings and rocky, armoured flesh. Their weakness would be their wings and rocky, armoured flesh which make them walking masquerade violations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:48:57-07:00","id":990113,"title":"","content":"I was thinking gargoyles could be a sub splat like ghouls. They themselves are like vampires because they need vampire bloods to keep moving. In my game I have two types ones created by kindred and free ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:47:36-07:00","id":990146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=989865#post989865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope I was talking nothing about masquerade. I saw the rules for creating gargoyles and being I was not sure how well it would work in 2e I've been using the horror rules to make them</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what exactly are you looking for when you speak of &quot;playable gargoyles&quot;? what take of them in Requiem books got your attention and what do they lack or suffer with that would make them unplayable as they currently are? Getting at the heart of the matter looks like the best place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T16:04:35-07:00","id":990152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990009#post990009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gargoyles aren't usually fit to play, but I'm sure you could whip something up to make them playable. I once started writing up a Coil that's fifth level could create Gargoyles that would be playable if you gave them a Humanity track, but I never got beyond the outline phase. Someday hopefully I'll finish you Coil of Genesis!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm heavily intrigued by this Coil, mind sharing a bit about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T05:04:11-07:00","id":990372,"title":"","content":"I don't really care about being able to play gargoyles, but I'd be interested if they made a comeback in 2e the way they were written in Danse Macabre. They were pretty varied and interesting and I only wished they made some more (although you could view them as sample gargoyles I guess). I like them because they make for really cool alternate enemies/security measures. A good thing to surprise players who are tracking down another vampire to their lair, expect maybe a fistfight and get ambushed by a towering monstrosity made of bones that can stab them from underground. A powerful ventrue with a big onyx lion walking around is also more intimidating. I never saw them as a big thing, but great whenever there was a need to show some of the weirder aspects of vampires or throw something unexpected.<br /> <br /> I mean, magical killbots (or messengers), I thought they were pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T05:40:36-07:00","id":990375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990152#post990152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm heavily intrigued by this Coil, mind sharing a bit about it?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, I'll just post the outline. Oh wow, this thing was written when Blood and Smoke first came out.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>The Mystery of Genesis</u></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blood is life, all vampires are aware of this. A select few are also aware that Vitae can be used to create new life, or at least a simulacrum of it in the form of gargoyles. Those who study the Mystery of Genesis do so in order to conquer the inherent sterility of the vampiric state and bring forth new unlife in their own image.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>The Coils of Genesis</u></b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Will of the Creator \u2022</span></span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Can Lash Out against gargoyles and sense them as if they were vampires.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Universal Conception \u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Can create gargoyles of different clans.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unbound Progenitor \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Uses full Blood Potency to determine the rank of gargoyle creatable, may not exceed rank 5.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bestowing the Fruit of Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>May give gargoyles the ability to enter torpor and exist after their master's death.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bestowing the Fruit of Knowledge \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Gives a gargoyle a virtue, vice, willpower tract and the ability to learn and grow.</i></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T06:57:39-07:00","id":990390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990375#post990375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure, I'll just post the outline. Oh wow, this thing was written when Blood and Smoke first came out.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>The Mystery of Genesis</u></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blood is life, all vampires are aware of this. A select few are also aware that Vitae can be used to create new life, or at least a simulacrum of it in the form of gargoyles. Those who study the Mystery of Genesis do so in order to conquer the inherent sterility of the vampiric state and bring forth new unlife in their own image.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><u>The Coils of Genesis</u></b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Will of the Creator \u2022</span></span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Can Lash Out against gargoyles and sense them as if they were vampires.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Universal Conception \u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Can create gargoyles of different clans.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unbound Progenitor \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Uses full Blood Potency to determine the rank of gargoyle creatable, may not exceed rank 5.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bestowing the Fruit of Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>May give gargoyles the ability to enter torpor and exist after their master's death.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bestowing the Fruit of Knowledge \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Gives a gargoyle a virtue, vice, willpower tract and the ability to learn and grow.</i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems cool. But can't vampires already lash out against things other then vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:19:51-07:00","id":990504,"title":"","content":"Would those coils modify the vampire's blood, the way the coils of the voivode does ? Then, feeding that blood to the gargoyle does the desired effect ? I'm thinking coils 1 to 3 are fine as coils, but 4 and 5 might work as scales instead, in which case, they'd be more like rituals/processes done to a gargoyle or as a modification to the process of gargoyle making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:02:19-07:00","id":990528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990390#post990390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems cool. But can't vampires already lash out against things other then vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. I suggest replacing the bit about Lashing Out with letting the vampire gain Blood Sympathy towards it's creation.<br /> <br /> I agree that the fourth and fifth Coils seems more fitting as Scales. Coils are exclusively about changing yourself, not others, and those changes are permanent (except when it comes to Draugr who automatically revert). To make them more thematic I'd either replace the last two Coils and have the current effects as Scales, or at least make them mandatory. A vampire with those Coils always uses them because they've changed how their blood works in the Birthing Ritual.<br /> I also wonder how the fourth Coil works in practice. Since a Gargoyle always requires the Vitae of their master according to the rules in The Danse Macabre, how would the Gargoyle be able to ever get out of Torpor? No matter how you solve it I think replacing a Gargoyle's master is an obvious Scale for this Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:26:53-07:00","id":990552,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry if it came across as unnecessary criticism, Xenorath. Do you mind if I take a shot at writing up an own version of your Coil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:39:49-07:00","id":990600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990390#post990390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems cool. But can't vampires already lash out against things other then vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that one is redundant. I probably didn't have a complete grasp on the new rules back then. Either that or there's a weird edge case I'm forgetting about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990504#post990504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would those coils modify the vampire's blood, the way the coils of the voivode does ? Then, feeding that blood to the gargoyle does the desired effect ? I'm thinking coils 1 to 3 are fine as coils, but 4 and 5 might work as scales instead, in which case, they'd be more like rituals/processes done to a gargoyle or as a modification to the process of gargoyle making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/989794-will-rules-on-gargoyles-get-updated?p=990552#post990552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if it came across as unnecessary criticism, Xenorath. Do you mind if I take a shot at writing up an own version of your Coil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it. I'd love to see it complete but like everything I start I'm much too lazy to actually finish it. It's not even that I find mechanics hard, I just can't bring myself to write what I come up with down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","user":"Xenorath","date":". 10-20-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:32:23-07:00","id":990681,"title":"","content":"Just a &quot;quick&quot; version of my own. I'm not quite sure how I would handle the fifth dot but I'm certainly leaning towards making the Gargoyle seem more like a Revenant, and I'd certainly add some flavour text describing rumours about a sixth Coil that turns them into an actual Vampire/Revenant. Of course, such a vampire would almost definitely become a draugr since it would lack the Humanity of an Embraced vampire. But that would also make my version of Gargoyles unplayable, which did not seem to be the intention of the thread's creator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Mystery of the Genesis</i></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><i>Coil of the Genesis</i></b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Spark of Progeny \u2022</b></i><br /> The Dragon has managed to instill a bit of themselves into their Creation, and thus taken the first step to mimic the Embrace. By expending a point of Willpower during the Birthing Ritual the Gargoyle gains Kinship with their creator. The Gargoyle counts as Once Removed for the purpose of Blood Sympathy. This connection is purely the Dragon and their Creation, and does not grant Blood Sympathy to the Dragon's relatives and clanmates. In addition the Gargoyle also exhibits the unmistakable Predatory Aura, though it does not allow it to focus their Aura and Lash Out.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Universal Conception \u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> The nature of the Birthing Ritual is not only known by the Dragon; it is part of them. The normal clan restrictions do not apply. Instead, the Dragon may create the specialized Gargoyles available to the other Clans as long as at least one Vitae used in the Birthing Ritual comes from a member of that clan.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Unbound Progenitor \u2022\u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> The innate mastery of the Birthing Ritual allows the Dragon to create more potent Gargoyles than normal. The maximum Rank of the Gargoyle is now the highest of the following; half the Dragon's Blood Potency rounded down, or the Dragon's dots in this Coil.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Bestowing the Fruit of Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> This Coil is the first reason a few Academies has outlawed the practice of this Mystery as it grants the Creation autonomy. Any Gargoyle after learning this Coil will no longer suffer the same fate as their master should they suffer a Final Death. It also no longer requires the sacrificed Vitae of its master to continue its existence. Instead it expends one Vitae every day to keep themselves active. They may gain Vitae from any vampire, and can hold five plus their Stamina dots Vitae to a maximum of ten. Voluntary or involuntary failure to expend this Vitae results in the Gargoyle falling into a Torpor from which it does not naturally awake. Only the order of its master (if it still contains Vitae) or being fed at least one Vitae will cause the Gargoyle to expend all its Vitae and awake. This Coil only takes effect should a point of Willpower be expended as described in Spark of Progeny.<br /> Researchers of this Mystery is quick to add that the Gargoyle still must follow the orders of its master, lest the Dragons find themselves practicing a forbidden Coil.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Bestowing the Fruit of Knowledge \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> *to be written*<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Sample Scales of the Genesis</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Succession of Supremacy</b></i><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coil:</b> Universal Conception<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> During the night of the month's first full moon the Dragon creates a solution from various rare ores and salts mixed with an amount of the master's Vitae equal to the master's Blood Potency. The master-to-be then drinks the solution without gaining any of the Vitae, and sacrifices the same amount of their own Vitae.<br /> <b>Outcome:</b> The mystical bond between the Gargoyle and its master has now been changed. It recognizes the Vitae sacrificed as their master's own Vitae, and adopts the new master with the same obedience. Should the Gargoyle require a monthly sacrifice this will be fulfilled for the coming month even if the Vitae sacrificed is less than the new master's Blood Potency.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d",