 though it does not allow it to focus their Aura and Lash Out.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Universal Conception \u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> The nature of the Birthing Ritual is not only known by the Dragon; it is part of them. The normal clan restrictions do not apply. Instead, the Dragon may create the specialized Gargoyles available to the other Clans as long as at least one Vitae used in the Birthing Ritual comes from a member of that clan.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Unbound Progenitor \u2022\u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> The innate mastery of the Birthing Ritual allows the Dragon to create more potent Gargoyles than normal. The maximum Rank of the Gargoyle is now the highest of the following; half the Dragon's Blood Potency rounded down, or the Dragon's dots in this Coil.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Bestowing the Fruit of Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> This Coil is the first reason a few Academies has outlawed the practice of this Mystery as it grants the Creation autonomy. Any Gargoyle after learning this Coil will no longer suffer the same fate as their master should they suffer a Final Death. It also no longer requires the sacrificed Vitae of its master to continue its existence. Instead it expends one Vitae every day to keep themselves active. They may gain Vitae from any vampire, and can hold five plus their Stamina dots Vitae to a maximum of ten. Voluntary or involuntary failure to expend this Vitae results in the Gargoyle falling into a Torpor from which it does not naturally awake. Only the order of its master (if it still contains Vitae) or being fed at least one Vitae will cause the Gargoyle to expend all its Vitae and awake. This Coil only takes effect should a point of Willpower be expended as described in Spark of Progeny.<br /> Researchers of this Mystery is quick to add that the Gargoyle still must follow the orders of its master, lest the Dragons find themselves practicing a forbidden Coil.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Bestowing the Fruit of Knowledge \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></i><br /> *to be written*<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Sample Scales of the Genesis</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Succession of Supremacy</b></i><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coil:</b> Universal Conception<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> During the night of the month's first full moon the Dragon creates a solution from various rare ores and salts mixed with an amount of the master's Vitae equal to the master's Blood Potency. The master-to-be then drinks the solution without gaining any of the Vitae, and sacrifices the same amount of their own Vitae.<br /> <b>Outcome:</b> The mystical bond between the Gargoyle and its master has now been changed. It recognizes the Vitae sacrificed as their master's own Vitae, and adopts the new master with the same obedience. Should the Gargoyle require a monthly sacrifice this will be fulfilled for the coming month even if the Vitae sacrificed is less than the new master's Blood Potency.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking good so far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}